OL,3,ABBC appeals against decision to allow
OL,4,ATrump's $10bn lawsuit to go ahead
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC has lodged an "urgent" appeal
OL,7,Fagainst a US judge's decision to allow
OL,8,FDonald Trump's $10bn (#7.6bn) lawsuit
OL,9,Fagainst the corporation to go ahead.
OL,11,FThe US president is suing the BBC for
OL,12,Fdefamation over the way an episode of
OL,13,FPanorama edited a speech he gave in
OL,14,FJanuary 2021, shortly before the riot
OL,15,Fat the US Capitol.
OL,17,FEarlier this month, a federal judge in
OL,18,FFlorida ruled that the defamation case
OL,19,Fcould proceed after the BBC sought to
OL,20,Fdismiss it.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG14/19
OL,24,ANext PageBCultureC Nat RadioFTechnology
FL,164,160,200,105,0,100
PN,11915
SC,0015
CT,25,T
PS,c000
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F119A1795634346
OL,1,W5j 5Q7+j 55"k#j 5w;js1
OL,2,W//%*// //%Q-.*,%-,* *,%%**,$ ,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,ABBC appeals against decision to allow
OL,4,ATrump's $10bn lawsuit to go ahead
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe BBC has now filed an appeal with a
OL,7,Fhigher court, saying there is a
OL,8,F"complete lack of evidence" that anyone
OL,9,Fin Florida accessed the programme, and
OL,10,Fthat the broadcaster made "rigorous and
OL,11,Fsystematic efforts to prevent access to
OL,12,Fthe documentary" in the US.
OL,23,APub: 25-NovQpppppppppppppppppppppG15/19
